Package: NetFunrankR
Type: Package
Title: Decomposed, Exact Network-Proximity Enrichment Analysis of Gene Lists
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("AKM", "Azad", email = "kazad@imamu.edu.sa",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5251-2214")),
    person("Mohammad Ali", "Moni", email = "m.moni@uq.edu.au",
        role = "aut"))
Description: Functional enrichment analysis of gene lists using shortest-path
    proximity in a protein-protein interaction network. The proximity of a
    gene list to each gene set is decomposed into a degree-aware overlap test
    and beyond-overlap tests of the non-member genes (number of linker genes
    and distance), conditional on the overlap. Null distributions follow the
    degree-preserving model of network medicine and are computed exactly by
    discrete convolution (saddlepoint approximation for long lists), so no
    permutations are required; the components are independent under the null
    and are combined with Fisher's method. The package bundles a STRING v12
    human interactome rebuilt without curated-database and text-mining
    evidence, KEGG, Reactome and WikiPathways libraries, plotting functions
    and an interactive Shiny dashboard.
